          "es": "Describe el mercado con metáfora, símil, personificación y una explicación."
        },
        "answer": {
          "text": "On a rainy Saturday the market was a grey river. People moved between the stalls like leaves in the water, and the rain danced on the roofs and whispered to the fruit. The lamps were golden apples in the dark morning, and the whole place breathed warm air. I chose the river because it shows how the crowd never stops moving. The sellers called their prices, and the smell of bread and coffee made everybody smile. It was a noisy, colourful place, and I felt happy and small in the middle of it, like a small boat on the river.",
          "accepted": [
            "On a rainy Saturday the market was a grey river. People moved between the stalls like leaves in the water, and the rain danced on the roofs and whispered to the fruit. The lamps were golden apples in the dark morning, and the whole place breathed warm air. I chose the river because it shows how the crowd never stops moving. The sellers called their prices, and the smell of bread and coffee made everybody smile. It was a noisy, colourful place, and I felt happy and small in the middle of it, like a small boat on the river.",
            "Yesterday the market was a big kitchen on a rainy day. The sellers shouted like cooks, and the crowd moved as slowly as a river between the stalls. The rain danced on the umbrellas and sang a quiet song. The fruit looked like small lamps, red and yellow and green. The smell of bread and coffee was a warm hug for everybody. I chose the kitchen because it shows how warm and busy the place was, even when the sky was grey. Everybody was wet, but everybody was smiling, and the market kept breathing until the evening."
          ]
        },
